  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4102.18 Automotive engine compartment adhesive",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4102.18 “Automotive engine compartment adhesive” means an aerosol adhesive designed for use in motor vehicle under-the-hood applications that require oil and plasticizer resistance, as well as high shear strength, at temperatures of 200 to 275 degrees Fahrenheit (°F).\n\nSource. #10527, eff 2-26-14; ss by #13969, eff 5-21-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4100.html"
